# Agent scratch, never committed. Both were un-ignored until the landing gate
# was mechanized, and `git add -A` therefore swept them into every clean
# export: .build holds the chair's and implementors' briefs, plans and logs
# (519 files / 4.8 MB when this was measured), and .wt is where a unit
# worktree is created, which `git add -A` records as a gitlink no file-count
# assertion can see. hack/gate/clean-export.sh asserts the exported tree's
# top-level entries against a literal allowlist as well — these two rules are
# the prevention, that assertion is the separate observer.
/.build/
/.wt/

# Go
/bin/
/dist/
*.exe
*.test
*.out

# local roster/secrets (never committed unencrypted; the age-encrypted
# roster itself is meant to be tracked once it exists)
*.local.toml
.env

# local roster + mutation-serialization lock state, written by running the
# binary against a real cluster; per-host, never shared
/pveforge.toml
/pveforge.toml.lock
/pveforge.toml.locks/
